  "reflection": {
    "what_people_were_focused_on": "Airlines were ordering new jets, music buyers were changing formats, and major diplomatic talks were beginning.",
    "what_actually_mattered": "Different businesses and markets delivered different results. Owning many companies helped avoid depending entirely on a struggling company such as IBM.",
    "what_faded_away": "Predictions that vinyl records were finished did not predict the returns of an electronics company or a whole stock market.",
    "what_nobody_knew": "The end of the Cold War and the precise company rankings were unknown. Strong demand in one industry was not a guarantee for every related investment.",
